{"ref":"BDB, מָמוֹת","hw":"מָמוֹת","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">מָמוֹת</span>]</big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] only pl. <strong>death (</strong>cf. Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">مَمَاتٌ</span> <strong>)</strong>;—cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְמוֹתֵי תַחֲלֻאִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 16:4\" href=\"/Jeremiah.16.4\">Je 16:4</a> of painful <em>death by diseases;</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ חָלָל</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 28:8\" href=\"/Ezekiel.28.8\">Ez 28:8</a>.—For <span dir=\"rtl\">הַמְּמוֹתִים</span> (Kt) <a data-ref=\"II Kings 11:2\" href=\"/II_Kings.11.2\">2 K 11:2</a>, <em>the slain</em>, Qr. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַמּוּמָתִים</span> is certainly correct (v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, מוּת\" href=\"/BDB,_מוּת\", dir=\"rtl\">מוּת</a> <strong>Hoph.</strong> supr.)","next":"BDB, תְּמוּתָה","prev":"BDB, (לְ)מוֹתָם"}